comments.message:
You can make this an input parameter if you want, but the rest of the code is on lines 26 and 29 are sort of hard-coding the behavior of deferring emitting signals until the object is created. So I think you can remove this constructor parameter. On line 28 you could do
```
bool skipSignal{true};
status(initialStatus, skipSignal);
```

Declaring a local in this case just makes the code more clear. Otherwise there is a hardcoded true second parameter, so the reader has to wonder what that does.
